  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was a tale of two stores with opposing momentum signals that demand your attention.\n\n**Port Washington is tracking well overall but hit a soft Monday.** Revenue down 20% day-over-day, but this was a capacity call, not a performance miss \u2014 you ran 3 groomers yesterday versus your typical 4, and those 3 delivered $513/groomer, above your trailing 30-day baseline of $504. The DOW-adjusted MTD number confirms real performance is sound: you're at $58,337 versus an expected $59,186, a negligible 1.4% miss. The bright spot: your 12+ week visit-cadence bucket just shrank from 15.5% to 13.3%, signaling retention is improving and customers are coming back more frequently. Your lapse pool of 496 customers represents $316K in recoverable annual value \u2014 that's real upside if reactivation lands.\n\n**Hicksville is flashing a warning light.** Yesterday's $1,047 revenue looks strong in isolation, but it's a compare-nothing baseline (last Monday was operational startup). More concerning: your 12+ week visit-gap bucket is *growing* \u2014 up from 10.2% to 12.6% \u2014 which is stealth churn. You're only scheduling 2 groomers through next week (versus Port's 34 groomer-days), and at $423/groomer-day MTD, you're running below your own trailing baseline of $413. Retail is holding (+58% YoY), but grooming attach (44%) is soft. Hicksville needs capacity injection or a reactivation push on that 84-person lapse pool.\n\n**Both locations have inventory gaps.** The X-Small Treat Table is out at both stores with high monthly velocity (34 and 39 units). Reorder now.\n\n**Capacity & coverage:** Port Washington has 6 groomers and 0 bathers scheduled today, 6 groomers and 7 bathers tomorrow; Hicksville has 2 groomers and 0 bathers both days; combined next 7 days: 47 groomer-days and 43 bather hours."
